Here is your updated `.gitignore` file with `.DS_Store` added for macOS, along with other standard additions for IDEs (like VS Code / Xcode), OS temporary files, and local build artifacts:

```gitignore
# Prerequisites
*.d

# Compiled Object files
*.slo
*.lo
*.o
*.obj

# Precompiled Headers
*.gch
*.pch

# Linker files
*.ilk

# Debugger Files
*.pdb

# Compiled Dynamic libraries
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.so.*

# Fortran module files
*.mod
*.smod

# Compiled Static libraries
*.lai
*.la
*.a
*.lib

# Executables
*.exe
*.out
*.app

# Build directories
build/
Build/
build-*/

# CMake generated files
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile
install_manifest.txt
compile_commands.json

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.log
*.bak
*.swp

# vcpkg
vcpkg_installed/

# debug information files
*.dwo

# test output & cache
Testing/
.cache/

# ==========================
# ADDED IMPORTANT EXCLUSIONS
# ==========================

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?

# Windows Explorer metadata
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# IDE & Editor specific configurations (VS Code, Xcode, etc.)
.vscode/
.idea/
*.xcodeproj/*
!*.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
*.xcworkspace/
.DS_Store
xcuserdata/

# Local Environment & User files
.env
.env.local
*.user

```